BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:United Nations Association Film Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T210000
DTSTAMP:20261022T120138Z
UID:dothebay-17927133@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:The 29th United Nations Association Film Festival continues We
 dnesday\, Oct. 21\, in San Francisco with an evening of documentaries expl
 oring identity\, addiction treatment and institutional accountability.\n\n
 The evening begins with "Becoming James\," directed by Evan Possley. The e
 ight-minute documentary follows a man who\, after decades in prison\, work
 s to rebuild his identity and finds success in an unexpected way.\n\nNext 
 is "Shuffle\," directed by Benjamin Flaherty. Through the filmmaker’s ow
 n recovery\, the documentary investigates the multibillion-dollar addictio
 n treatment industry\, examining financial incentives\, conflicts of inter
 est and the system surrounding people seeking treatment.\n\nThe evening co
 ncludes with "Nuns vs. The Vatican\," directed by Lorena Luciano and produ
 ced by Filippo Piscopo. The film follows a former Catholic nun who breaks 
 her silence about abuse within the Church\, as other nuns come forward to 
 examine a culture of silence and institutional protection.\n\nUNAFF runs O
 ct. 15–25\, 2026\, with the theme Passion for Change. The festival featu
 res films on human rights issues like the environment\, women’s rights\,
  racism\, and peace\, engaging a diverse Bay Area audience. More info at u
 naff.org.\n\n$19\nUnited Nations Association Film Festival\n\nDetails: htt
 ps://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/21/united-nations-association-film-festiv
 al-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com
 /future-day-comedy-show-claudia-wells-jennifer-parker-film/
GEO:37.7843591;-122.3885501
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34821763/00c97041-b8a9-4e96-8d06-e61644c3336e.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261022T120138Z
LOCATION:Delancey Street Screening Room\, 600 The Embarcadero\, San Franci
 sco\, CA\, 94107
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/21/united-nations-association-film
 -festival-tickets
END:VEVENT
