BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Filipiñana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T223000
DTSTAMP:20261023T114720Z
UID:dothebay-17930193@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Director Rafael Manuel in person for introduction and Q&A mode
 rated by Ali El-Sadany\, editor of FilmSlop\, on Saturday\, September 5 (a
 t rush).\n\nPresented by FiliKula\n\nAmid stifling heat and pervasive drou
 ght\, Isabel (Jorrybell Agoto)\, a 17-year-old Ilokana from the rural nort
 h\, works at a posh country club outside Manila\, lining up golf balls for
  powerful men to drive into the verdant horizon. New to the job\, she wand
 ers the immaculate grounds sampling its luxuries as members\, including an
  industrialist and his expatriate niece\, the club president and his pampe
 red wife\, and a slew of Chinese tourists\, engage in a complex dance with
  the club’s doting and subservient staff. But something is rotting benea
 th the pristine fairways of the elite resort\, as Isabel discovers when sh
 e tries to return a mislaid golf club to its patriarchal director\, Dr. Pa
 lanca (Teroy Guzman). The deeper she journeys into its most exclusive corn
 ers\, the closer she gets to the violent truths of the club\, her native P
 hilippines\, and her own past..\n\n“A masterwork…with Filipiñana\, Ma
 nuel opens new vistas in the future of the cinema.” – The New Yorker\n
 \n“An invigorating dose of arch formalism in a sea of mainstream sinceri
 ty\, this is the kind of movie that asks for the viewer’s attention…th
 e angle of a golf club can evoke suspense\, a piece of fruit on the ground
  can feel like a tragedy\, and a casual glance can take your breath away.
 ” – Vulture\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 40m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirector\n\nRafael
  Manuel\n\nFormat\n\nDCP...\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/1
 0/22/filipinana-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
