BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Playing with Fire: An Ecosexual Emergency
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTSTAMP:20261026T131406Z
UID:dothebay-17856338@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Beth Stephens & Annie Sprinkle IN PERSON!\n\nPlaying with Fire
 : An Ecosexual Emergency is a joyous ecosexual documentary born from the a
 shes of California’s devastating fires. When lightning ignites the redwo
 od forest\n\nsurrounding their home in Boulder Creek\, longtime lovers Bet
 h Stephens and Annie Sprinkle are forced to evacuate — and their lives a
 re forever transformed.\n\nThey blend loss and grief into ecosexual art\, 
 moving through fire as destructive\, regenerative\, and erotic forces\, wh
 ile fusing humor\, community care\, social justice and environmental\n\naw
 areness into a lush and fiery journey of transformation.\n\nThe film unfol
 ds through an ecosexual lens (imagining the Earth as a lover) while weavin
 g stories from formerly incarcerated firefighters\, an Indigenous scholar\
 , fire artists\, neighbors\, a witch-therapist\, a fire-play massage fetis
 hist\, and a fire tassel twirling burlesque queen.\n\nPartially narrated b
 y Boulder Creek’s mythical white peacock Albert and culminating in a cer
 emonial Wedding to Fire on a riverbank in the redwoods\, Playing with Fire
  is a creative\n\nand urgent call-to-action as the climate crisis worsens\
 , and is a powerful portrait of queer resilience in the face of a world in
  flames.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 11m\n\nYear\n\n2025\n\nDirector\n\nAnnie Sprinkl
 e & Beth Stephens\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nUSA\n\nLanguage\n\nEnglis
 h\n\nFirst Showing\n\nOctober 25\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nFeatured\n\nDetai
 ls: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/25/playing-with-fire-an-ecosexual-
 emergency-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34488706/1e7eb492-c030-4e6f-a3e3-e726d6942c18.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261026T131406Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/25/playing-with-fire-an-ecosexual-
 emergency-tickets
END:VEVENT
