CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Juno FilmsGerman cinema helped give birth to horror with class
 ics like Nosferatu and The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari\, and a new generation 
 of filmmakers is reviving that tradition today. After last year’s look a
 t the genre films of the 1970s\, this year we turn to the zombie\, one of 
 horror’s most versatile figures and often read as an allegory for confor
 mity\, racism\, and capitalism.\nRammbock: Berlin Undead (Dir. Marvin Kren
 \, Germany 2010\, 63 min.)\nHeartbroken Michael comes to Berlin to return 
 his ex-girlfriend’s keys and ends up trapped in her apartment building d
 uring a zombie outbreak. This was Germany’s very first zombie film.\n\nE
 ver After / Endzeit (Dir. Carolina Hellsgård\, Germany 2018\, 90 min.)\nA
 fter a zombie epidemic\, two very different women flee from Weimar to Jena
 \, one of the last safe cities. Along the way\, they discover that nature 
 has taken over the world. The film is based on Olivia Vieweg’s graphic n
 ovel and was made by an all-female crew.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.e
 ventbrite.com/e/halloween-screening-zombie-films-tickets-2003222085182\nDe
 tails: https://sf.funcheap.com/halloweenscreening-zombie-films-sf/\nSource
 : Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screen
 shot-2026-10-13-135604.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T050002Z
LOCATION:Goethe-Institut San Francisco\, 657 Howard Street San Francisco\,
  CA 94105
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/halloweenscreening-zombie-films-sf/
END:VEVENT
