SUMMARY:Film Screening: Kikuyu Land
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTSTAMP:20261026T045612Z
UID:dothebay-17996536@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Watch a special screening of Kikuyu Land\, a new documentary c
 o-directed by Emmy Award-winner Andrew H. Brown and Nairobi journalist Bea
  Wangondu. Released in January 2026\, the documentary has been nominated f
 or awards at Sundance Film Festival\, Seattle International Film Festival 
 and The Hague Movies that Matter Festival.\n\nSet in Kenya's tea highlands
 \, the documentary follows Mr. Mungai\, a local claimant pursuing justice 
 for land taken from his family. What begins as a personal claim soon revea
 ls a deeper web of historical erasure\, as his fight brings him into confl
 ict with a powerful multinational corporation still operating on contested
  ground. As Mungai's case gains momentum\, it draws in Bea\, a local news 
 producer\, whose investigation uncovers buried histories and long-silenced
  family truths. Their paths expose how the legacy of the empire continues 
 to shape lives in the present. Running alongside this struggle is the stor
 y of Stephen\, the son of a tea worker\, whose childhood unfolds within th
 e very plantations at the center of the dispute. His daily life makes clea
 r that this history is not in the past but ongoing.\n\nFree\n\nPresented b
 y San Francisco Public Library\n\nFree\nSan Francisco Public Library\n\nTi
 ckets: https://on.sfpl.org/KikuyuLand\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/event
 s/2026/11/1/film-screening-kikuyu-land-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
