SUMMARY:El Sett (Opening Night of the 30th Arab Film Festival)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T200000
DTSTAMP:20261026T203423Z
UID:dothebay-17998364@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:The 30th Arab Film Festival opens with Marwan Hamed’s sweepi
 ng portrait of Umm Kulthum\, the most iconic Arab singer of all time.\n\nB
 efore the film\, Guest of Honor Mohamed Hefzy receives the very first AFMI
  Luminary Award for Cultural Impact. After it\, Aswat Ensemble takes the s
 tage with a live tribute to her music.\n\nJoin us in your best evening att
 ire\, just as you would have dressed to see Umm Kulthum at her legendary 1
 967 concert at the Paris Olympia. There will be plenty of chances to have 
 your photo taken\, so let’s make the evening a tribute to the most iconi
 c Arab singer of all time.\n\nPlease note: Some scenes have a strobing eff
 ect that may affect photosensitive viewers.\n\nThe flagship event of the A
 rab Film and Media Institute (AFMI)\, the Arab Film Festival is the longes
 t running and largest independent festival of its kind in North America.\n
 \nThis year\, join us from Nov.5th to Nov 14th for a program that will spa
 n 10 days\, presenting over 40 films from 26 countries\, over 30 directed 
 by women. AFF30 will also include opportunities to get together\, a classi
 c film\, industry and community panels\, filmmaker Q&As and more. Select p
 rograms will also be simultaneously presented online.\n\nFor more details\
 , visit arabfilmfestival.org\n\nhttps://aff30.arabfilmfestival.org/events#
 opening-night\nThe 30th Arab Film Festival presents:\n\nTickets: https://a
 ff30.arabfilmfestival.org/events#opening-night\nDetails: https://dothebay.
 com/events/2026/11/5/el-sett-opening-night-of-the-30th-arab-film-festival-
 tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/30
 th-arab-film-festival-sfs-amc-kabuki-nov-514/\n- https://arabfilmfestival.
 org/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca
