SUMMARY:Free “Wood Street” Film Screening on Oakland’s Unhoused + Q&
 A (SF Main Library)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
DTSTAMP:20261020T194441Z
UID:funcheap-1643321@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Caron CreightonWOOD STREET follows a year in the life of Oakla
 nd’s largest unhoused encampment as its residents face an imminent evict
 ion that threatens to dismantle their community. As notices appear and pol
 ice move in\, residents organize — building barricades\, filing lawsuits
 \, and protesting at City Hall to fight for their right to stay. Told thro
 ugh immersive verité\, the film places viewers inside the encampment\, ca
 pturing the urgency\, resilience\, and emotional toll of collective resist
 ance. At its center are John and LaMonté\, whose bond is tested as pressu
 re mounts — LaMonté’s mental health deteriorates while John struggles
  to remain sober. When the eviction comes\, the community is physically er
 ased\, but its spirit endures.\nThe film will be followed by a Q&A with th
 e film team\, members of the Wood Street community and the editor of Stree
 t Sheet newspaper.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://sfpl.org/events/2026/11/07/
 film-wood-street-post-film-discussion\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/fr
 ee-wood-street-documentary-screening-community-qa-sf-main-library/\nSource
 : Funcheap SF
