BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edward Said: Between Worlds (Bay Area Premiere)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T194500
DTSTAMP:20261026T203423Z
UID:dothebay-17998256@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:As part of the 30th Arab Film Festival\, join us for the Bay A
 rea Premiere of Edward Said: Between Worlds\, an archival documentary exam
 ining the life\, ideas\, and enduring legacy of Palestinian-American schol
 ar\, author\, and public intellectual Edward Said.\n\nTold through archiva
 l material and Said’s own words\, the film follows his journey from his 
 childhood in Jerusalem and displacement in 1948 through his academic caree
 r at Columbia University and his emergence as one of the twentieth century
 ’s most influential cultural critics and advocates for the Palestinian p
 eople.\n\nStay after the film for a panel discussion with director Maiken 
 Baird\, producer Sarah Mowaswes\, and Edward Said’s family\, moderated b
 y Dr. Ussama Makdisi.\n\nThis screening is co-sponsored by the Palestinian
  & Arab Studies Program at UC Berkeley.\n\nThe flagship event of the Arab 
 Film and Media Institute (AFMI)\, the Arab Film Festival is the longest ru
 nning and largest independent festival of its kind in North America.\n\nTh
 is year\, join us from Nov.5th to Nov 14th for a program that will span 10
  days\, presenting over 40 films from 26 countries\, over 30 directed by w
 omen.\n\nAFF30 will also include opportunities to get together\, a classic
  film\, industry and community panels\, filmmaker Q&As and more. Select pr
 ograms will also be simultaneously presented online.\n\nFor more details\,
  visit arabfilmfestival.org\n\nhttps://aff30.arabfilmfestival.org/events#c
 enterpiece\nThe Arab Film Festival presents:\n\nTickets: https://aff30.ara
 bfilmfestival.org/events#centerpiece\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events
 /2026/11/8/edward-said-between-worlds-bay-area-premiere-tickets\nSource: D
 oTheBay
