SUMMARY:Henry: Portrait of a Serial Killer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T194500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T214500
DTSTAMP:20261023T171442Z
UID:dothebay-17979566@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:One of the most harrowing films of the 20th century\, HENRY is
  just as much in conversation with SEX\, LIES\, AND VIDEOTAPE as it is wit
 h THE TEXAS CHAIN SAW MASSACRE or DAWN OF THE DEAD. It’s right up there 
 with key works by Haneke\, Cronenberg\, and Noé in its effortless ability
  to push the audience in directions it never thought it’d go. Presaging 
 both our current true-crime obsession and “elevated arthouse horror\,”
  this shockingly audacious debut by John McNaughton (WILD THINGS)\, with i
 ts chilling career-defining turn by Michael Rooker (“The Walking Dead”
 \, GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY)\, has inspired multiple generations of filmmak
 ers to go for the throat. (AGFA)\n\nNew 4K restoration courtesy of the Ame
 rican Genre Film Archive\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show/terror
 -tuesday-henry-portrait-of-a-serial-killer?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=22947\n
 Details: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/10/henry-portrait-of-a-serial
 -killer-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
