BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All About My Mother
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T191500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T211500
DTSTAMP:20261023T171442Z
UID:dothebay-17979568@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Presented in Spanish with English subtitles\n\nThough Pedro Al
 modóvar’s films have pushed the boundaries of cinema as far back as the
  mid-1970s\, it wasn’t until 1999’s ALL ABOUT MY MOTHER that the Acade
 my Awards finally took notice\, naming it the Best Foreign Language Film o
 f the year. And it serves as a perfect encapsulation of his enduring power
  as an artist: it’s colorful\, dynamic\, emotional\, darkly funny\, and 
 imbued with profound empathy.\n\nWhen tragedy strikes\, Manuela (Cecilia R
 oth\, PEPI\, LUCI\, BOM) travels to Barcelona for the first time in years 
 in search of someone from her past. But she is waylaid by her old friend A
 grado (Antonia San Juan)\, a transgender sex worker\, as well as new frien
 ds\, such as Hermana (Penélope Cruz\, PAIN AND GLORY)\, a nun with a secr
 et\, and Huma (Marisa Paredes\, THE SKIN I LIVE IN)\, an actress performin
 g in town. Together\, the women form a unique bond that carries them throu
 gh the challenges that life throws at them.\n\nDriven by the powerhouse pe
 rformances of each actress in the film\, ALL ABOUT MY MOTHER showcases the
  humanity of these women at their best and worst\, their highest and lowes
 t\, resulting in a portrait of friendship\, family\, and love that is sing
 ularly Almodóvar.\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show/all-about-my
 -mother?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=22950\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/event
 s/2026/11/13/all-about-my-mother-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35067887/144b5f08-adcc-4d65-ba54-f82ed1fe8055.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T171442Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/13/all-about-my-mother-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Searchers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T143000
DTSTAMP:20261023T171442Z
UID:dothebay-17979584@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:A favorite film of some of the world's greatest filmmakers\, i
 ncluding Martin Scorsese and Steven Spielberg\, THE SEARCHERS has earned i
 ts place in the legacy of great American films for a variety of reasons. P
 erhaps most notably\, it's the definitive role for John Wayne as an icon o
 f the classic Western – the hero (or antihero) who must stand alone acco
 rding to the unwritten code of the West.\n\nAs with many of Ford's classic
  Westerns\, THE SEARCHERS must contend with revisionism in its stereotypic
 al treatment of "savage" Native Americans\, and the film's visual beauty (
 the final shot is one of the great images in all of Western culture) is co
 mpromised by some uneven performances and stilted dialogue. Still\, this i
 s undeniably one of the greatest Westerns ever made.\n\nTickets: https://d
 rafthouse.com/sf/show/the-searchers?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=22951\nDetails
 : https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/the-searchers-tickets\nSource: Do
 TheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35067991/a38d7ef6-efb6-4a06-971d-e963fe63dd52.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T171442Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/the-searchers-tickets
END:VEVENT
