DESCRIPTION:What happens when great actors collide with the worst script e
 ver written? Tommy Wiseau's original THE ROOM (2003) infamously burned thr
 ough $6 million and months of shooting with no-name actors. This reimagini
 ng flips the myth on its head. Filmed in under 12 hours\, on virtually no 
 budget\, with Bob Odenkirk (Better Call Saul)\, Bella Heathcote (THE NEON 
 DEMON)\, executive producer Mike Flanagan (The Haunting of Hill House)\, a
 nd directed by newcomer Brando Crawford. With no rehearsal and only telepr
 ompters to guide them\, the cast embraced the chaos with Shakespearean gra
 vity\, transforming cinematic disaster into unpredictable spectacle – al
 l for charity.\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show/the-room-a-tribu
 te?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=23198\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/202
 6/11/25/the-room-returns-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
