 nderson\nPresented in 35mm\n\nWednesday\, December 2 | The Castro\n\nCamer
 on Winter\, in December 2025\, after a months-long sold-out tour with his 
 band Geese\, returned to New York to play a single show at Carnegie Hall. 
 This is the movie.\n\nDirected and shot on 35mm and 16mm by Oscar-winning 
 filmmaker Paul Thomas Anderson (One Battle After Another)\, the crew inclu
 des filmmaker and actor Benny Safdie (The Smashing Machine) and music prod
 ucer Ariel Rechtshaid (Grammy winner for albums with Vampire Weekend and A
 dele).\n\nGQ praised Cameron Winter’s show at Carnegie Hall as “stagge
 ringly good\,” and Nick Cave said he has a “a glorious\, emotive voice
  with brilliant\, blistering words\, a racked and wondrous thing.” Winte
 r’s solo album Heavy Metal was named one of the best of the year by Pitc
 hfork\, Rolling Stone\, Paste and Mojo and Geese’s last record Getting K
 illed was named the best album of 2025 by The New Yorker\, NME\, and Stere
 ogum.\n\nAll Ages\nSold out\nAnother Planet Entertainment presents\nListed
