SUMMARY:Eyes Wide Shut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T140000
DTSTAMP:20261023T171442Z
UID:dothebay-17979576@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:In IT’S A WONDERFUL LIFE\, Jimmy Stewart’s George Bailey\,
  at the height of his suicidal despair and panic\, imagines a world in whi
 ch he doesn’t exist. Stanley Kubrick goes one step further in sending To
 m Cruise down an odyssey of sexual confusion and paranoia to learn the tru
 e meaning of Christmas.\n\nAdapted from the Austrian short story Traumnove
 lle\, Kubrick’s final film peeks us into the privileged world of Dr. Bil
 l Hartford and his wife Alice (Cruise and Nicole Kidman)\, two well-to-do 
 attractive socialites who\, by all accounts\, have it made. In a marijuana
 -fueled argument\, Alice reveals thoughts of infidelity that send Bill int
 o an existential panic\, leading to an absurdist walkabout through New Yor
 k that involves – you guessed it – a mysterious sex cult run by a shro
 uded aristocracy.\n\nDid Kubrick make this to break up Cruise and Kidman
 ’s marriage? How much did he know about mysterious sex trafficking rings
 ? Did Sydney Pollack originate the shirtless-in-suspenders look? Clearly\,
  the film poses more questions than it answers. For certain\, EYES WIDE SH
 UT is a brutally funny sexscapade that puts an ellipses at the end of Kubr
 ick’s storied career – and\, most importantly – stands as a crucial 
 text for our modern world. Fidelio!\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/
 show/queer-film-theory-101-eyes-wide-shut?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=23199\nD
 etails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/12/eyes-wide-shut-tickets\nSou
 rce: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35067950/9ff46f3b-5714-45b3-84f1-15d71ba0b774.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T171442Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/12/eyes-wide-shut-tickets
END:VEVENT
